Subject: [PATCH] 3731 / BN: the approved line goes out word for word; the
 referral lines decline the names
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Box 52869 (1 of 2). BN ran correctly in both trios — task_asks.question held
„ბექა შუამავლიძემ შენ გირჩია. ანა მთხოვნიძე ეძებს დახმარებას: …" — but every
ask passes the outgoing editor (D711), which for a relay is told the asker
is the helper and has no owner words; in trio 1 it rewrote the line into
„ბექა შუამავლიძეს სჭირდება დახმარება: …", dropping „შენ გირჩია" and the real
asker. Trio 2 passed, edited too („ეძებს" → „სჭირდება").

- createAskNow takes approvedWording: text Misho approved word for word is
  sent as written and never edited. Only BN's own line sets it, through
  createRelayAsk; every other ask is edited as before.
- askReferral's four Georgian lines wrote „<name>-ს", „<name>-ისთვის"; they
  now use geoName („თამარ ნოტარიძეს", „ანა მთხოვნიძისთვის"). Same words.

The glued footer could not be reproduced from the stored text (the „?" and
the blank line before the footer are there); asked the tester which screen.

